Raon-1-mini-preview oracle prompts (tools/ref/raon1-dump.sh): token ids, one decimal id a line, no BOS (the file's add_bos_token is
false, so llama-tokenize adds none). The dumper never tokenizes (tools/ref/cb_dump.cpp): a tokenizer difference would read as a
kernel bug.

Made once, on the box, by the tokenizer of the dump's own tree (KRAFTON's llama.cpp branch raon-1-mini-preview at
fb895662d25868756a19253ca5e0688f99b18994, /home/user/llama.cpp-raon, CPU build, libllama.so md5 fcd56f0bf8345d9d1ce89e4b713d5ed8) on
the Q4_K_M file (vocabulary only; the pre-tokenizer is `raon`):

    llama-tokenize -m <file> -f <text> --ids --no-escape --log-disable     # "[id, id, ...]", written one id a line

