    The cuts are of the texts tools/ref/data/minimaxm3 and solar2 are made from (full a, b, c: sha256 db8af4d0..., beb7baf5...,
    c7990d34..., /home/user/stage/sorc/prompts/{a,b,c}.txt). The model ends a finished sentence with its end token (llama-simple, CPU, greedy, on the
    full a: 30 of 32 tokens, on the full b: 0), and the dumper's greedy loop runs a fixed number of steps past it, so the prompts end
    mid-sentence: each of the cut texts decodes the full 32 tokens without the end token.
    The texts hold no backslash, so --no-escape and the default tokenize alike.

d is 1,536 ids: more than the RDA scan's 16-position chunks (the per-channel gate's chunk size) and an MLA context beyond a single ubatch's 512 rows (three ubatches).
